{"created": "2026-10-24T19:12:19.185446+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T19:12:19.582728+00:00", "id": 23624565, "conceptrecid": "23624411", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624565", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624411", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624565", "metadata": {"title": "Packing k\u00b2 \u2212 \u2308\u221a(32k)\u2309 \u2212 1 unit squares in a square of side less than k", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624565", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>Let s(N) be the side of the smallest square containing N unit squares with disjoint interiors, and let c*(k) be the largest c with s(k&sup2; &minus; c) = k. We prove c*(k) &lt; 4&radic;(2k) + 1 for every integer k &ge; 6, that is, s(k&sup2; &minus; &lceil;&radic;(32k)&rceil; &minus; 1) &lt; k. The construction is Ryu's L-shaped packing: an aligned grid and two bands of b tilted rows. Both ends of each band are filled with axis-parallel rows, and b is the odd integer nearest &radic;(2k). The odd width keeps the rounding loss of each filled end below 3/2. The same idea and the same constant 4&radic;2 were found earlier by Evan Daniel, who proves c*(k) &le; 4&lceil;&radic;(2k &minus; 7)&rceil; &minus; 1 for every k &ge; 7 in Lean (https://github.com/evand/square-packing, certificates/k2-minus-c/, 18 October 2026); for k &ge; 89 the two integer bounds differ by at most 2. This note is an independent second proof, with a different split of the free length and an odd band width. Exact rational certificates for k &le; 600 are checked by two independently written programs.</p>\n<p>Version 0.2 credits Daniel's earlier result and removes the claim, made in version 0.1, that this was the smallest explicit bound known. Files: the note as PDF (draft v0.2, 5 pages) and its LaTeX source. Code, exact certificates and checkers: https://github.com/TheSnakeFang/squarepack-certs/tree/b1b3f6bda13739c9eeecc1ceaefec9178294e0ca/theorem-a</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Fang, Kevin", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["square packing", "unit squares", "Erd\u0151s\u2013Graham", "combinatorial geometry", "exact certificates", "c*(k)"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/TheSnakeFang/squarepack-certs/tree/b1b3f6bda13739c9eeecc1ceaefec9178294e0ca/theorem-a", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23278927", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23463481", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "0.2", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23624411"}}]}}, "title": "Packing k\u00b2 \u2212 \u2308\u221a(32k)\u2309 \u2212 1 unit squares in a square of side less than k", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624565", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624565", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624565?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624565", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624565", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23624565", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624565/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624411", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624411", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624411", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23624411", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23624565/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23624565/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624565/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624565/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/